                        "review": "[code]\n[table]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Gameplay[/td]\n        [td]■ . . . . . . . . .[/td]\n        [td]1/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Graphics[/td]\n        [td]■ ■ ■ ■ ■ ■ ■ . . .[/td]\n        [td]7/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Atmosphere[/td]\n        [td]■ ■ ■ ■ . . . . . .[/td]\n        [td]4/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Game depth*[/td]\n        [td]■ . . . . . . . . .[/td]\n        [td]1/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Game length         [/td]\n        [td]■ . . . . . . . . .[/td]\n        [td]1/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n[/table]\n\nVR specific:\n[table]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Immersion[/td]\n        [td]■ ■ ■ ■ ■ ■ ■ ■ . .[/td]\n        [td]8/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Physical activity[/td]\n        [td]■ ■ ■ . . . . . . .[/td]\n        [td]3/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Motion sickness risk[/td]\n        [td]■ ■ ■ ■ ■ ■ . . . .[/td]\n        [td]6/10[/td]\n    [/tr]\n[/table]\n[/code]\n* Don't get confused - actual depth bellow player on the plank is huge :)\n\n+ Surprisingly nice graphics for such short experience\n+ Great immersion if you actually walk on a physical plank while playing this (I also recommend a fan to simulate wind)\n+ Great easy-to-use introduction into VR\n\n- Very short experience (about 10 minutes)\n- No options or level selection, the only interaction is catching birds (which is not a big problem if experience lasts only a few minutes)\n\n• You can play it even with smaller area than the store page says it requires\n\n[b]Movement[/b]: \t\tNone (just roomscale), Automatic (in some levels, player moves with the plank)\n[b]Controls[/b]: \t\tMotion controllers\n\n[b]My progress[/b]: \t\t0.5 hours, finished (3x)\n[b]Recommended price[/b]: \t3 € (if you have more people around to try it; it is too short to be worth the price for one-use only)\n\n[u]My overall recommendation score: [b]65%[/b][/u]\n\n\n[url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/nachtomvr#curation]More reviews of VR games here! (NachtomVR - Steam curator)[/url]",
